{
  "an4.39:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.39 ",
  "an4.39:0.2": "4. Situations ",
  "an4.39:0.3": "With Ujjaya ",
  "an4.39:1.1": "Then Ujjaya the brahmin went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an4.39:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: ",
  "an4.39:1.3": "“Does the worthy Gotama praise sacrifice?” ",
  "an4.39:1.4": "“Brahmin, I don’t praise all sacrifices. ",
  "an4.39:1.5": "Nor do I criticize all sacrifices. ",
  "an4.39:1.6": "Take the kind of sacrifice where cattle, goats and sheep, chickens and pigs, and various kinds of creatures are slaughtered. ",
  "an4.39:1.7": "I don’t praise that kind of violent sacrifice. ",
  "an4.39:1.8": "Why is that? ",
  "an4.39:1.9": "Because neither perfected ones nor those who are on the path to perfection will attend such a violent sacrifice. ",
  "an4.39:2.1": "But take the kind of sacrifice where cattle, goats and sheep, chickens and pigs, and various kinds of creatures are not slaughtered. ",
  "an4.39:2.2": "I do praise that kind of non-violent sacrifice; for example, a regular gift as a propitious sacrifice. ",
  "an4.39:2.3": "Why is that? ",
  "an4.39:2.4": "Because perfected ones and those who are on the path to perfection will attend such a non-violent sacrifice. ",
  "an4.39:3.1": "Horse sacrifice, human sacrifice, ",
  "an4.39:3.2": "the sacrifices of the ‘casting of the yoke-pin’, ",
  "an4.39:3.3": "the ‘royal soma drinking’, and the ‘unbarred�